Aggressive Cows
You are given an array with unique elements of stalls[], which denote the positions of stalls. 
You are also given an integer k which denotes the number of aggressive cows. 
The task is to assign stalls to k cows such that the minimum distance between any two of them is the maximum possible.


Explanation:

🧮 Overall Strategy

  Sort the stall positions
  Binary search on distance
  For each mid distance:
  Check if cows can be placed using a greedy approach
  Store the largest valid distance

🐄 Greedy Placement Logic (Very Important)
  To check if a distance d is possible:
  Place the first cow at the first stall
  Always place the next cow at the earliest stall that is at least d distance away
  This greedy choice ensures we place cows as far apart as possible
  If we can place all k cows → distance d is valid.


Logic to check if we can place the cows
First we place cow 1 at the the 0th index of stalls -> stalls[0] -> this is termed as lastpos. Keep a track of number of cows, so initally count_cows=1;
run through the stalls array and check if the stalls[i]-lastpos >= d (the distance).
if so bring lasptos to stalls[i] and increase the count of cows. 
if all cows are placed , return true, else return false.

Now to find the maximum of maximum distances between cows.
WHat we have to do is, first identify the range of possible distances. it is from 1 to maximum number in the stalls array of distances.
then use BS and check the logic to place cows
if true, the ans=mid and shift left to mid+1 to check the next maximum, else right to mid-1;




Code:
class Solution {
    public int aggressiveCows(int[] stalls, int k) {
        // code here
        int n=stalls.length;
        Arrays.sort(stalls);
        // The ranges of distance will be from 1 -> max distance number in the stalls distances
        int left=1;
        int right=stalls[n-1]-stalls[0];
        
        int ans=-1;
        
        while(left<=right){
            int mid=(left+right)/2;
            if(canPlaceCows(stalls,k,mid)==true){
                ans=mid;
                left=mid+1;
            }
            else{
                right=mid-1;
            }
        }
        return ans;
        
    }
    
    public boolean canPlaceCows(int[] stalls, int cows, int d){
        int n=stalls.length;
        int lastpos=stalls[0]; 
        int cows_placed=1; // 1 cow is alread placed at index 0;
        for(int i=0;i<n;i++){
            if(stalls[i]-lastpos>=d){
                cows_placed++;
                lastpos=stalls[i];
            }
        }
        
        if(cows_placed>=cows){
            return true;
        }
        else{
            return false;
        }
    }
}
